    <div class="beat"><span class="beat-label">The move</span><p>Pulled your <code>/endpoints</code> feed on 2026-08-20 — 30 endpoints for <code>deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731</code>, with per-token price, quantization, context, max output, and 1-day uptime — and cross-checked against Artificial Analysis and DeepInfra's own pages.</p></div>
    <div class="beat"><span class="beat-label">The detail</span><p>The chart below. The cheapest endpoint on the page was $0.065/M fresh input — fp4 at 262K context. The real full-context fp8 pool started at roughly $0.067–$0.084. And the <em>most expensive</em> endpoint in the set was also fp4 with a truncated 262K/131K window. Price does not encode quality in either direction.</p></div>
    <div class="beat"><span class="beat-label">Point</span><p>You treat "same model ID" as a hypothesis to be tested, not an assumption — which is the whole job of a research scientist at a router.</p></div>
