<section id="guardrails">
  <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">08</span><h2>Don't overclaim these</h2></div>
  <p class="sec-sub">Five places where the precise version is both true and more impressive than the loose version.</p>

  <div class="warn">
    <h3>The inference product never launched</h3>
    <p>Say <em>prototype, gates open</em> — not "I ran an inference business." It runs locally, passes 16 tests, dry-runs to a 61.8&nbsp;KiB bundle, and has never taken customer traffic. Written downstream-resale permission from OpenRouter was a launch gate <strong>and I never obtained it</strong>. Volunteering that reads as judgment, and it's the correct answer to give someone whose terms you'd have needed.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="warn">
    <h3>The Terminal-Bench numbers are a partial snapshot</h3>
    <p>Roughly half the suite was still pending and the two legs were at different depths. Quote the setup, not the means — or quote the means with "in progress" attached every single time.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="warn">
    <h3>Every price is a catalog claim on a date</h3>
    <p>Use exactly that phrasing. All the endpoint numbers came from a live feed on 2026-08-20; none were contracts, and some had already drifted a day later. This is a framing OpenRouter will recognize immediately as correct.</p>
  </div>

